## Summary

When creating a workspace via Clone, the git clone operation can take 14+ seconds. During this time, the submit button becomes disabled via `!canSubmit` (which includes `!isSubmitting`) and the text changes to "Creating..." — but the only visual change is `opacity: 0.5`, which is nearly imperceptible on the colored primary button. Users see no clear feedback that their action is in progress.

The fix adds an inline spinner to the submit button during submission (matching the established GitActionBar pattern) and keeps the button at full opacity so the loading state is unmistakable.

## Technical Approach

**Approach: Inline spinner inside the submit button + submission-specific disabled styling**

The codebase has an established pattern for button loading indicators: an inline `<span className={styles.spinner} />` rendered conditionally inside the button alongside the text (see GitActionBar.tsx lines 79, 93, 108, 123, 136, 169, 200). This is a CSS-only border-based spinner with `animation: spin 0.8s linear infinite`. We follow the same pattern here.

The key insight from the bug report is that `opacity: 0.5` on a primary-colored button with white text is nearly invisible. During submission, the button should remain fully opaque so users can clearly see "Creating..." + the spinner. We use a separate `.submitting` class for this state instead of relying on `:disabled` alone.

**Trade-offs considered:**
- A full-modal overlay with spinner was considered but is overkill — the button spinner pattern is already used throughout the app
- A progress bar was considered but git clone doesn't emit progress data through the current API, so it would just be indeterminate (same as a spinner)
- Disabling all form fields during submission is already done (inputs have `disabled={isSubmitting}`) which is good — this fix focuses on making the submit button state obvious

