4. Clicking the Reopen button sets the issue status to "open" via the existing API (same as selecting "Open" from the dropdown)
5. While a status change is in-flight (from either the button or the dropdown), the Close/Reopen button shows "..." and is disabled
6. If the status change API call fails, an error toast appears (existing behavior from handleStatusChange)
7. The Close/Reopen button must NOT appear when the panel is in read-only mode (no `onStatusChange` prop)
8. The Close button uses danger/red styling; the Reopen button uses info/blue styling
9. Both buttons have correct aria-labels: "Close issue" and "Reopen issue"
10. Both buttons are keyboard accessible (focusable, Enter/Space triggers click, focus-visible ring)
11. The button's data-testid values are "header-close-issue-button" and "header-reopen-button" (distinct from "header-close-button" which is the panel close X)
12. The button must NOT appear in the full-page IssueDetailView — only in the side panel's IssueHeader

