**Props:**
\`\`\`typescript
interface DiffFilePanelProps {
  filePatch: DiffFilePatch | null;
  loading: boolean;
  error: Error | null;
  selectedPath: string | null;
  comments: InlineComment[];
  onAddComment: (filePath: string, lineNumber: number, content: string) => void;
  onRemoveComment: (commentId: string) => void;
}
\`\`\`

**Implementation:**
- Fills remaining horizontal space (flex: 1), overflow-y auto
- **No file selected:** Show centered placeholder "Select a file to view changes"
- **Loading:** Show loading indicator
- **Error:** Show error message with retry suggestion
- **Binary file (filePatch.is_binary):** Show "Binary file — cannot display diff"
- **Too large (filePatch.is_too_large):** Show "File too large to display"
- **Code/text file (default):** Parse and render using react-diff-view:

\`\`\`tsx
import { parseDiff, Diff, Hunk, getChangeKey } from 'react-diff-view';
import 'react-diff-view/style/index.css'; // base styles

// Parse the unified diff patch
const files = parseDiff(filePatch.patch, { nearbySequences: 'zip' });

// For single-file patches, files[0] contains hunks and type
const { hunks, type } = files[0];

// Build widgets map for inline comments
const widgets: Record<string, ReactElement> = {};
for (const hunk of hunks) {
  for (const change of hunk.changes) {
    const key = getChangeKey(change);
    const lineComments = comments.filter(c => c.lineNumber === change.lineNumber);
    if (lineComments.length > 0) {
      widgets[key] = (
        <InlineCommentThread
          comments={lineComments}
          onRemove={onRemoveComment}
        />
      );
    }
  }
}

// Render
<Diff viewType="split" diffType={type} hunks={hunks} widgets={widgets}>
  {hunks => hunks.map(hunk => <Hunk key={hunk.content} hunk={hunk} />)}
</Diff>
\`\`\`

- **Comment interaction via gutterEvents:**
  \`\`\`tsx
  const gutterEvents = {
    onClick(event: { change: Change }) {
      // Show inline comment form at this change's line
      setCommentingAt(getChangeKey(event.change));
      setCommentingLine(event.change.lineNumber);
    }
  };

  // Pass to Hunk: <Hunk hunk={hunk} gutterEvents={gutterEvents} />
  \`\`\`
  When the user clicks a gutter line number, a small inline form (textarea + submit/cancel) appears as a widget at that line. Submitting calls \`onAddComment(selectedPath, lineNumber, content)\`. The form state (\`commentingAt\`, \`commentingLine\`, \`commentText\`) is local to DiffFilePanel.

- **Custom gutter rendering** via \`renderGutter\` prop on Hunk:
  - Show a subtle "+" icon on hover for lines without comments
  - Show a comment count badge for lines with existing comments

- **react-diff-view CSS override:** Import the library's base CSS (\`react-diff-view/style/index.css\`), then override specific classes in DiffFilePanel.module.css to match the project's CSS variable theme:
  - Font: var(--font-family-mono)
  - Font size: var(--font-size-xs) or 13px
  - Addition background: var(--color-success-bg)
  - Deletion background: var(--color-danger-bg)
  - Gutter colors matching theme

- **Empty patch:** If \`filePatch.patch\` is an empty string (no changes), show "No changes in this file"

