## Summary

Integrate the DiffViewer component (from loomcli-947qg.4) as a new \"Diff\" tab in the AgentDetailPanel slide-out panel. This involves extending the TabType union, adding a third tab button, lazy-loading the DiffViewer via React.lazy/Suspense, and widening the panel to 1100px when the Diff tab is active via a data-wide attribute. This is the final integration piece that makes the diff viewer feature accessible from the agent detail view.

## Technical Approach

**Minimal changes to AgentDetailPanel.tsx:** Extend the existing two-tab pattern to three tabs. The DiffViewer is lazy-loaded at the component level (not at App.tsx level) using React.lazy + Suspense, matching how MonitorDashboard lazy-loads UsageDashboard internally. This keeps the DiffViewer bundle out of the AgentDetailPanel chunk.

**Panel widening via data attribute:** Add a `data-wide` attribute to the `.panel` aside element when activeTab === "diff". CSS targets `[data-wide]` to override max-width from 840px to 1100px. This is cleaner than inline styles and follows the existing data-attribute patterns in the codebase (data-state, data-mode, data-active, etc.).

**Tab reset behavior:** The existing useEffect resets to "info" tab when agentName changes (line 160-162). This stays as-is — the diff tab won't persist across agent switches, which is the correct UX.

**Lazy loading conditional:** The DiffViewer's `enabled` prop should be false when the diff tab isn't active, preventing unnecessary API calls. The React.lazy import only triggers when the diff tab is first selected.

