## Edge Cases & Error Handling

1. **Null issueDetails**: The updateIssueDetails function handles prev being null by returning null (no-op).
2. **Concurrent updates**: If the user rapidly changes status, each mutation returns the latest server state. The last response wins, which is correct.
3. **Failed mutation**: handleStatusChange already catches errors and shows statusError. On failure, onIssueUpdate is not called, so the UI correctly stays at the old value.
4. **Title/priority edits**: handleTitleSave (line ~570) and handlePrioritySave (line ~608) also call onIssueUpdate, so they benefit from the same fix for free.
5. **IssueDetailView**: The full-page detail view (IssueDetailView.tsx) does NOT have inline status/title editing — it renders read-only badges. No changes needed there for this bug. If inline editing is added later, the same pattern applies.

