5. **Merge skips unmatched agents**: Set up git agents ["alpha", "beta"] and daemon entries ["alpha" only]. Verify `agents[0]` (alpha) has daemon fields, `agents[1]` (beta) has all daemon fields `undefined`.
6. **Merge with empty daemon entries**: Set up git agents with daemon entries `[]`. Verify all daemon fields on all agents are `undefined`.
7. **Merge only runs on dual-fetch success**: Mock daemon fetch to reject. Verify `agents[0].supervisor_status` is `undefined` (merge not called).
8. **Merge clears stale daemon fields**: First fetch: daemon succeeds (daemon fields populated). Second fetch: daemon fails (dvegl.6 degraded mode). Verify agents in second fetch have `undefined` daemon fields (not stale values from first fetch).
9. **Legacy mode (no workspaceId)**: Start polling without `workspaceId`. Verify `agents[0].supervisor_status` is `undefined` (merge not called).

**`src/stores/__tests__/mergeDaemonFields.test.ts`** — Direct unit tests for the helper (optional, if the function is exported):

