**Props interface:**

```typescript
export interface CommentItemProps {
  /** The comment to display */
  comment: Comment;
  /** Reactions on this comment */
  reactions?: CommentReaction[];
  /** Current user identifier for permission checks (e.g., "web-ui") */
  currentUser?: string;
  /** Issue ID (needed for API calls) */
  issueId: string;
  /** Called after comment text is successfully edited. Parent should update its state. */
  onCommentUpdated?: (updatedComment: Comment) => void;
  /** Called after comment is successfully soft-deleted. Parent should update its state. */
  onCommentDeleted?: (commentId: number) => void;
  /** Called when user clicks Reply. Parent sets replyTo state for CommentForm. */
  onReply?: (commentId: number) => void;
  /** Called after a reaction is toggled. Parent should refresh reactions for this comment. */
  onReactionsChanged?: (commentId: number) => void;
  /** Called when user clicks the add-reaction button. Parent wires up ReactionPicker (hfsf0.7). */
  onAddReactionClick?: (commentId: number) => void;
  /** Additional CSS class name */
  className?: string;
}
```

**Internal state:**

```typescript
const [isEditing, setIsEditing] = useState(false);
const [draftText, setDraftText] = useState(comment.text);
const [isSaving, setIsSaving] = useState(false);
const [isDeleting, setIsDeleting] = useState(false);
const [confirmingDelete, setConfirmingDelete] = useState(false);
const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);
const textareaRef = useRef<HTMLTextAreaElement>(null);
```

**Reaction grouping (useMemo):**

```typescript
interface GroupedReaction {
  emoji: string;
  count: number;
  authors: string[];
  currentUserReacted: boolean;
}

const groupedReactions = useMemo(() => {
  if (!reactions || reactions.length === 0) return [];
  const groups = new Map<string, { count: number; authors: string[] }>();
  for (const r of reactions) {
    const existing = groups.get(r.emoji);
    if (existing) {
      existing.count++;
      existing.authors.push(r.author);
    } else {
      groups.set(r.emoji, { count: 1, authors: [r.author] });
    }
  }
  return Array.from(groups.entries()).map(([emoji, { count, authors }]) => ({
    emoji,
    count,
    authors,
    currentUserReacted: authors.includes(currentUser ?? ""),
  }));
}, [reactions, currentUser]);
```

**Key handlers:**

- `enterEditMode()`: Sets isEditing=true, draftText=comment.text, error=null. Guarded: only if comment.author === currentUser and !comment.deleted_at.
- `cancelEdit()`: Sets isEditing=false, resets draftText, clears error.
- `saveEdit()`: Trims text. If unchanged, exits edit mode. Otherwise: setIsSaving(true), call editComment(workspaceId, issueId, comment.id, trimmedText). On success: setIsEditing(false), call onCommentUpdated with updated comment (spread comment with new text and edited_at = new Date().toISOString()). On error: show error, stay in edit mode, refocus textarea. Finally: setIsSaving(false).
- `handleDelete()`: If !confirmingDelete, set confirmingDelete=true and return. If confirmingDelete: setIsDeleting(true), call deleteComment(workspaceId, issueId, comment.id). On success: call onCommentDeleted(comment.id). On error: show error, setConfirmingDelete(false). Finally: setIsDeleting(false).
- `cancelDelete()`: Sets confirmingDelete=false.
- `toggleReaction(emoji)`: Determine if currentUser already reacted with this emoji (from groupedReactions). If yes: call removeReaction(workspaceId, issueId, comment.id, emoji). If no: call addReaction(workspaceId, issueId, comment.id, emoji). On success: call onReactionsChanged(comment.id). On error: show brief error (set error, clear after 3s timeout).
- `handleKeyDown(e)`: Cmd/Ctrl+Enter → saveEdit(). Escape → cancelEdit(). (Only active in edit mode.)

**Render logic (3 branches):**

**Branch 1 — Tombstone (comment.deleted_at is truthy):**
```jsx
