### Backend parent_id support for addComment
The existing `handleAddComment` handler (handlers_comments.go) reads only `text` from the request body via `AddCommentRequest{Text string}`. It does not read `parent_id`. For the reply feature to actually create threaded comments in the database, the backend handler must be extended to:
1. Add `ParentID *int64 \`json:"parent_id"\`` to the handler's `AddCommentRequest` struct
2. Call `storage.AddIssueCommentWithParent(ctx, issueID, author, text, parentID)` instead of `storage.AddIssueComment(ctx, issueID, author, text)` when parentID is non-nil
3. The RPC layer (OpCommentAdd / CommentAddArgs) may also need updating to pass parent_id

