export type LoomAgentStatus = Omit<
  components["schemas"]["MonitorAgentStatus"],
  "workspace"
> & {
  /** Workspace name from daemon config (empty string in legacy/single-repo mode) */
  workspace?: string;
  /** Whether agent works across multiple repos */
  cross_repo?: boolean;
  /** Absolute path to the agent's working directory */
  path?: string;
  /** Absolute path to the agent's worktree */
  worktree_path?: string;

  // --- Daemon supervision fields (populated by workspace-scoped endpoint) ---
  /** Process ID of the agent's session */
  pid?: number;
  /** Raw daemon supervisor status: "running" | "stopped" | "failed" | "starting" */
  supervisor_status?: string;
  /** Number of times the daemon has restarted this agent */
  restart_count?: number;
  /** Error classification from the last failure */
  last_error_class?: string;
  /** ISO timestamp when the current backoff expires */
  backoff_until?: string;
  /** Reason the agent was stopped (user-initiated, error, etc.) */
  stop_reason?: string;
  /** Task ID from the agent's lock file (active work) */
  task_id?: string;
  /** Epic ID assigned to this agent */
  epic_id?: string;
  /** Whether a yield has been requested for this agent */
  yield_requested?: boolean;
  /** Reason for the yield request */
  yield_reason?: string;
  /** ISO timestamp when the yield was requested */
  yield_requested_at?: string;
  /** Count of uncommitted file changes (number, not the changes array) */
  changes_count?: number;
};
```

Key decisions:
- All new fields are optional (?) — zero breakage for existing consumers
- Types use string for ISO timestamps (not Date) — matches JSON transport and avoids parse overhead. Components that need Date objects can parse on demand.
- supervisor_status is string (not a union type) — the backend may add new statuses; treating it as an open string avoids needing a type update for each new status value. The YieldIndicator component (task .14) will narrow it locally.
- changes_count is a separate field from the existing changes (MonitorFileChange[]). The workspace endpoint returns a count; the monitor endpoint returns the full file list. Both can coexist — some UIs need the count, others need the details.

