## Summary

Make agent control routes workspace-scoped by replacing the flat `AgentControlFn` on `ServerConfig` with a resolver-based dispatch: `AgentControlResolverFn func(wsID string) (AgentControlFn, error)`. Each handler extracts the wsID from `middleware.WorkspaceFromContext(r.Context())`, calls the resolver to obtain a workspace-specific control function, and invokes it. This eliminates the silent-CWD bug where `POST /api/workspaces/{ws}/agents/{name}/stop` (and the four other routes) ignored `{ws}` because `BuildAgentControlFn` captured `os.Getwd()` at construction and dialed the initial workspace's `daemon.sock` for every request.

